<worksheet >
    <title>EIPO-2 Diagonalization</title>
  <introduction>
    <p>To earn an M on this outcome, complete both problems. 
      Complete problem 1 with progress on problem 2 to earn a P.</p>
  </introduction>  
   <page>
      <exercise>
    <p>Let <md alignment="alignat" alignat-columns="1">
      <mrow>A=\begin{bmatrix}-4 &amp; 3\\ 0 &amp; -1\end{bmatrix}</mrow>
    </md> for <m>k \in \mathbb{R}</m>. Find an invertible matrix <m>P</m>
    and a diagonal matrix <m>D</m> such that <m>A=PDP^{-1}</m>.</p>
  </exercise>
  </page>
  <page>
  <exercise>
    <p>Let 
      <md alignment="alignat" alignat-columns="3">
        <mrow>A= \begin{bmatrix}3 &amp; 0 &amp; 0\\0 &amp; -1 &amp; 0\\0 &amp; 0 &amp; 3\end{bmatrix}</mrow>
      </md> Find <m>A^4</m>.</p>
  </exercise>
  </page>
</worksheet>